WEBVTT

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.860
Did you decide what you're 
gonna be for the play?

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.430
We can choose whatever we want, right?

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:18.710
I... I wanna be Magi-Girl, or Yoshiko-chan.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:20.700
It's gotta be Yoshiko-chan.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.910
I'm gonna be Mr. Galigali!

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:25.880
Huh?

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:30.860
Tsumugi-chan, the teacher told us 
to pick from this list, remember?

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.380
Mr. Galigali's on the list!

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.890
<b>Yoshiko</b>

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:34.940
See?

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.890
That's just part of the picture.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.420
Yoshiko-chan's cute.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.220
Let's be her together.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.690
If you want to be Mr. Galigali,

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:49.520
it must be 'cause you're weird.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.150
Wh-Why would you say that?

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.220
Let's go, Yuuka-chan.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.440
Why?

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.710
New rice. Maitake mushrooms.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.310
Sweet potatoes...

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:13.370
Salmon...

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.640
Long live fall, the season of bounty!

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.560
Iida-san looks like she's 
enjoying her lunch, as usual.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:29.980
She looks so happy.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.040
It must really be good.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.790
She's making me so curious.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:35.320
Me, too...

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.450
Hey, the second-years say 
they're doing a crêpe stand, too!

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.270
What?!

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.160
Then we're doing the same thing?

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.140
What the heck?

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.480
Crêpes...

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:20.470
<b>A Play and Sweet Potato Crêpes</b>

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.440
Um...

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:26.100
So it's already been decided that 
our class is doing a crêpe stand,

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.140
<b>Cultural Festival Crêpe Stand</b>

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:29.140
but there are two other 
classes doing crêpe stands,

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:33.230
and they're all ready to add
maid outfits and cosplay to theirs.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.340
Are they seriously doing maid outfits?

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:38.520
The second-years are doing 
ladies' basketball cosplay.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.440
Whoa! Bet they'll look tough!

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:44.160
Is there anything we can do 
to make ourselves stand out?

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.460
That's what I'd like us to discuss now.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.960
Put the girls in swimsuits?

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:49.790
Good idea!

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:50.910
Heck no.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.290
The guys can do that.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.120
Put on suits and wear glasses.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.250
What the heck?

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.070
Oh, jeez!

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:00.210
If it's within our budget, it can just
be a new menu item or something!

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.100
Hey, hey, Iida-san.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.080
Do you have any ideas?

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.080
M-Me?

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.020
Yeah!

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.630
They said it could be a new menu item.

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:15.060
Oh, right!

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.570
Iida-san's mom is that chef...

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:20.650
Is it okay to talk about that?

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.610
I've been wondering, too!

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.490
I knew it!

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.120
She's the one on TV, right?

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.840
M-My mom's a good chef,

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:30.320
but I don't really cook...

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.820
But you like eating, right?

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:34.620
She sure does, right?

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.710
Right?

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:41.610
So can you think of any really yummy crêpes

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.380
you want to eat right now?

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:47.390
A crêpe I want to eat...

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.110
May I have some time to think?

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:06.460
Okay, so we'll come up with 
a new idea for a crêpe!

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:09.170
Iida-san, can you look into it for us?

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:10.170
Leave it to me.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.610
Crêpes, huh?

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.820
The last time I ate one was...

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.820
Come to think of it,

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.220
Tsumugi's never had a crêpe.

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:37.670
My first crêpe was handmade by Daddy!

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.640
That would be great.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.110
That's a great idea.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.830
Why don't we have a taste-testing party?

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:52.060
Let's do it!

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:53.960
What should we make?

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:55.390
It's fall...

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:56.680
Mackerel pike, maybe?

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:59.370
No, maybe not...

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:00.580
Some kind of potato?

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:02.340
Oh, that might work!

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:09.430
There.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:12.210
Tsumugi...

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.930
I was talking to Kotori-san today.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.000
Is something wrong?

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.020
Nope.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:21.440
Okay...

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:24.650
Hey, Tsumugi,

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.440
you've never had a crêpe, right?

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:28.430
A crêpe?

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:30.060
Yeah, a crêpe.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:32.000
They're sweet and delicious!

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.280
We're going to be making some soon!

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:37.930
I'm sure you'll love them!

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:42.330
All you talk about is food, Daddy!

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.840
Talk about girls!

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.840
T-Talk about girls?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:50.940
Jeez!

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:51.900
Tsumugi?

00:06:57.010 --> 00:06:58.540
Come on out of there.

00:06:58.540 --> 00:06:59.270
Come on.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:05.520
What's wrong?

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:08.280
I see.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.340
That girl, Hana-chan...

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:13.800
She wants to play the same part as you, right?

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:14.660
Yeah.

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:18.660
I don't think she said it just to be mean.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:21.460
She really just wanted to be friends.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:24.750
I think so...

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:31.260
You have to tell your friends and the teacher 
that you really want to be Mr. Galigali.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.740
I'll talk to them tomorrow, too.

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:35.670
Is that okay?

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:41.510
Okay, now you can talk about crêpes!

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:43.850
Oh, uh... Thanks.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.020
Okay!

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:50.650
Then we'll have Tsumugi-chan be Mr. Galigali.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:54.300
Sorry to make such a selfish request.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:57.120
No, we're the ones who are sorry.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:00.720
Let's all have a fun play, okay?

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:02.460
Understand, you two?

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:03.260
Yeah.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:04.840
Yeah.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:07.790
Then let's have a make-up handshake.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:21.700
Hey, Hana-chan...

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:30.990
I'm home!

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:31.900
Tsumugi?

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.700
How'd it go today?

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:37.320
Were you able to get along with your friend?

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:38.460
Yeah...

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:39.160
I see.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:46.600
Tsumugi...

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.640
If you're still having problems...

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:50.340
I'm not!

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:54.970
I can't wait to eat some crêpes!

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:59.180
Crê-crê-crê! Pe-pe-pe!

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.970
I can't wait!

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.260
Hello!

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:16.570
Welcome!

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:18.870
Huh? Yagi's here, too?

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:22.040
Wow, why? Why are you here?

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:25.400
I wanted some friends' opinions, too.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:28.170
I was asked to supply ingredients.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:32.480
Yagi-chin claims he's good at making 
sweets, so I brought him here.

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:33.640
Like as an advisor?

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:34.920
Drop the "chin."

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:37.340
Y-You guys are friends?

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:38.400
No.

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:40.670
Her family's where I get my ingredients.

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:41.930
And she found out.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:45.730
Everyone's here!

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:47.950
She's happy.

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:51.060
It really is fun with more people around.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:52.110
I'm glad.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:54.920
Tsumugi was feeling a little down.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.470
Hey, are we having a party today?

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:00.430
That's right!

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:02.120
A crêpe party!

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:03.740
<b>Crêpe ingredients are something like this!</b>

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:09.380
<b>Whipped Cream

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:09.380
<b>Crêpes: About 10 

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.960
I did a lot of thinking, and...

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:05.980
It's fall,

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:07.200
and they're good,

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:08.940
and they're easy to get, so...

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:11.840
I settled on delicious sweet potatoes!

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.840
<b>Take the milk 
out of the fridge 
and let it warm to 
room temperature first.</b>

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.840
<b>Sweet Potato Cream 

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:14.680
I can't wait!

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.380
Okay, we'll start with the dough!

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:18.750
Come on, give it a try!

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.110
You can do it! You can do it!

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:21.350
Okay!

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:26.310
Let's see... We need the milk at room 
temperature, so we'll set that out now.

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:31.360
Put the butter in the frying pan you'll use 
for the crêpes, and heat it on medium.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:35.930
Sizzly!

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:38.530
The butter smells amazing.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.820
Once the bubbling stops

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:42.910
and it's turned faintly brown,

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:44.310
take it off the heat.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:46.690
About like this?

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:47.660
That'll do.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.960
Let it cool on a damp cloth.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:56.170
Then sieve the flour you've 
measured out into a bowl.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.010
Like this?

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.720
I'll do it next.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:12.150
Let me see that.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.330
It's faster to do it this way.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.740
W-Well, give it a try.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:22.450
Okay!

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:25.280
Put in the granulated sugar

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:26.840
and the eggs.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.820
Make a hole for the eggs 
in the center of the flour,

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:31.040
and drop them in there.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:33.800
We're gonna put the butter in. Can you grab it?

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:34.500
Okay!

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.710
Crê-crê-creeey!

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.420
Crê-crê-creeey!

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:42.000
Crêpe-pepe-pe!

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.220
Batta-batta-butter!

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:46.540
Is that a crêpe song?

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:48.100
No!

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:51.850
It's a make-crêpes-yummy song, 
to make crêpes yummy!

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:54.310
Well, we gotta have that!

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:56.060
Right?

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:59.070
Once you add the milk and stir,

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:01.780
put it somewhere cool for an hour.

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:06.200
Tsumugi-chan sang the make-crêpes-yummy song,

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.320
so they're gonna taste great!

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:09.690
I can't wait!

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:11.740
But Tsumugi,

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:14.620
you've never had a crêpe, right?

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:17.050
What?

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:18.420
I know about them, though!

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.820
They're like this, right?

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:22.490
See?

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:26.310
That's... a... crêpe?

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:30.000
Daddy talked about them all the time,

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.480
so I learned!

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:35.450
D-Did I talk about them that much?

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:37.130
You did!

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:41.120
Daddy talks about food a lot.

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:42.610
Especially lately.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.390
He doesn't talk about girls.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.970
Only about food.

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:59.390
Ts-Tsumugi-chan, look at me!

00:12:59.390 --> 00:13:02.140
I like food even more!

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:03.340
How does that help?

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.050
That's pretty funny.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:08.490
Hey.

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:13.710
I don't know what happened, 
but don't take it out on other people.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:17.640
All your dad ever thinks about is you.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:24.270
Is that how it looks?

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:25.160
It is.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:26.080
It is!

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:26.950
It sure is!

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:30.100
I don't know if that's how it looks,

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:33.410
but you're all I ever think about, Tsumugi.

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:42.040
I see!

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:45.420
Sorry for being a bad Tsumugi.

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:46.720
It's okay.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.360
Thanks.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:55.600
Now, let's make the filling 
while we let the dough rest.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:56.430
Okay!

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:57.890
I'll help, too!

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:03.110
Peel the sweet potatoes, then cut them
into two- or three-centimeter pieces.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.360
It's so hard...

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:14.410
Good work!

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:16.480
Let Daddy handle the rest.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:17.830
It's all yours.

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:20.440
Tsumugi-chan...

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:23.960
Were you okay with the knife?

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:25.910
You weren't scared?

00:14:25.910 --> 00:14:27.300
Nope!

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.000
I... I see...

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:30.620
What's wrong?

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:33.260
Nothing!

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:39.050
Okay, the next step is to soak the sweet potato 
bits in water for about ten minutes,

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:41.520
then cover with plastic wrap and microwave

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:44.260
for five minutes, with a tablespoon of water.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:49.610
When you can stick a toothpick 
clean through them, they're done.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:51.820
Use a masher to smash them up.

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:56.330
So this mysterious tool is called a masher?

00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:59.290
This is how you use it?

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:02.250
Add the granulated sugar,

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:05.800
then add boiled milk a little 
at a time, and stir to finish.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:08.100
The dough should be ready by now.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.360
Fry the crêpe dough!

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:18.570
It's spreading!

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:19.810
It's spreading!

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:23.770
Once the edges turn brown, turn it over...

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:24.480
Ow, hot!

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:25.480
Hot!

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.360
Now let's whip the cream, too!

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:38.650
Tsumugi-chan, let's wrap the crêpes together.

00:15:38.650 --> 00:15:39.500
Okay!

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:44.730
Today we'll wrap them up like 
envelopes, not in a triangle.

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:46.460
They're soft!

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.460
They're pretty sturdy, though.

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:50.470
It's done!

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:54.720
The sweet potato crêpes are done!

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:56.460
So these are crêpes?

00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:57.580
They sure are!

00:15:57.580 --> 00:15:58.570
These are crêpes!

00:15:58.570 --> 00:15:59.860
Let's eat them!

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:00.770
Okay!

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:14.610
It's so sweet...

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:17.080
It's good.

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:21.540
The sweet potatoes and cream
give it a really smooth taste.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:23.790
I love sweet potatoes...

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:26.590
The crêpe dough is so chewy and yummy!

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:27.870
It's so sweet.

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:29.910
I added some rum to the mash for mine.

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:35.010
Crêpes are so good, huh?

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:39.870
I think I can present this to my class.

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:41.300
Your class?

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:45.900
Yeah, we're having a festival 
called the cultural festival.

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:51.110
And we were saying we wanted to come 
up with a new kind of crêpe to sell.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:53.110
<b>Cultural Festival Crêpe Stand</b>

00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:53.870
The people in my class

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:57.410
knew that I like to eat,

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:02.540
so they came to me for help.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:05.900
I've never really talked to them,

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:08.120
but they knew what I liked.

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:11.070
So you know,

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:14.620
if I can make everyone happy 
by doing what I like,

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:17.050
that makes me really happy.

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:19.810
You don't know they'll be happy yet.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:21.560
Don't say that! It's too scary!

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.170
I'm jealous...

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:28.440
What I like

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:31.690
doesn't make my friends happy.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:38.110
Tsumugi, that's not true.

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:45.400
What is that?

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:47.080
What's that thing?

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:50.880
I got the idea while watching you make 
outfits for the cultural festival.

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:53.200
Pink fluffy-fluff!

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:57.220
I'm going to make a Mr. Galigali 
outfit for the play.

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.260
Mr. Galigali?

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:03.800
If there's something you want to do, 
that's important to me.

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:06.210
But Hana-chan said

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:09.080
she wanted to be Yoshiko-chan with me.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:11.900
Maybe when she sees the outfit, she'll say,

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.940
"Wow, that's great!"

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:16.710
No, I don't know about that.

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:18.910
I hope she does!

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:22.160
Tsumugi, listen.

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:29.730
Sometimes things go badly, even if 
nobody really did anything wrong.

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:30.800
Yeah.

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:33.920
But there are still things you can try,

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:38.120
so why don't you work 
a little harder with Daddy

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:39.930
to get Hana-chan to understand?

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:42.300
Yeah!

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:47.390
I think I like working hard!

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:50.060
'Cause making food is fun!

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:54.980
I'll work hard, okay?

00:18:58.020 --> 00:18:59.360
It's so good!

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:01.550
Okay, let's work hard!

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:03.870
Yeah! Gimme seconds!

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:07.740
Morning!

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:09.250
Good morning!

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.210
Good morning, Hana-chan!

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:13.300
Morning.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:16.670
Wait! Look at this!

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:31.990
M-Mr. Galigali?

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:32.730
Yup!

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.300
It's Mr. Galigali!

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:35.420
It's so cute!

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:35.710
Did you make it?

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:39.040
Daddy made Mr. Galigali for me!

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:40.490
Wow!

00:19:40.930 --> 00:19:44.760
Anybody who's Yoshiko-chan 
can put their hand in here!

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:46.740
Just like on TV?

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:49.130
Go ahead.

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:51.450
I can?

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:52.200
Yup!

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.530
I'm gonna be Mr. Galigali,

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:08.970
so Hana-chan, will you be in the 
play with me as Yoshiko-chan?

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:10.810
Okay!

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:13.370
This is gonna be the best play ever!

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:14.600
Right?

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:17.110
I'm so glad...

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:22.030
<b>Shikizou High School Cultural Festival</b>

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:25.700
<b>Crêpes 
250 Yen</b>

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:25.700
<b>Sweet Potato Cream
Handmade!</b>

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:29.780
Once the edges turn brown, flip it over.

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:33.680
Perfect!

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:34.620
I did it!

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:36.580
Okay, let's get cooking!

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:40.210
It's so soft and sweet!

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:42.350
The sweet potato is great!

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:43.630
This is Heaven!

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:46.680
The end of the line for the crêpe stand is here!

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:49.610
Try our most popular crêpe: 
sweet potato cream!

00:20:49.610 --> 00:20:52.010
You can't get it anywhere else but here!

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:53.770
Iida-san.

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:01.880
Iida-san, you really do make a great witch!

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:05.280
I-I'm really supposed to go outside in this?

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:08.440
All the girls doing advertising 
and accounting are dressing up.

00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:09.850
Let's go!

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:11.700
O-Okay...

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:13.290
<b>Yummy Sweet Potato Crêpes</b>

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:15.580
Yummy sweet potato crêpes!

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:18.250
<b>Yummy Sweet Potato Crêpes</b>

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:18.250
Only available here!

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:20.960
Th-They're good...

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:22.880
We have crêpes!

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:26.090
<b>Play</b>

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:29.760
Yoshiko-chan! Put your hand into my fluff!

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:31.880
Hooray! Fluffy-fluff!

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:33.770
Got it, Mr. Galigali!

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:37.480
Hooray! Fluffy-fluff!

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:41.770
There are more Mr. Galigalis...

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:43.870
Thank you, Magi-Girl!

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:46.070
Recording

00:21:43.870 --> 00:21:45.100
Thank you!

00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:55.960
Great job!
